  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run (1 of the 6-run budget used): 8 witnesses passed and the rule calls no other rules.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_130.lean`)\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a member of `DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle`.\n- **When it applies:** the bicycle's speed is above `p.halt_speed_tolerance`.\n- **Obligation:** speed × speed ≤ 2 × deceleration × (distance seen − speed × `p.bicycle_reaction_time`). Writing it as a product keeps the measured speed and visibility out of any divisor. Since a rule's only allowed literal is zero, the factor 2 is written as a term added to itself.\n- **Deceleration:** a selection by `Term.cond`: the ice value on ice or snow; otherwise the wet value on a wet road or in precipitation; otherwise the dry value.\n- **Distance seen:** the record says to use visibility, or in darkness the smaller of visibility and the headlamp reach. I wrote this as two checks: the bound must hold at visibility, and in darkness also at the headlamp reach. A longer distance only makes the bound easier to meet, so this says exactly what the record says. I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_130.lean`): one bicycle rides east for three instants, with every environment field the rule reads set.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | 6 m/s, dense fog, 10 m visibility | violated |\n| `permit` | 5 m/s, dry road, daylight, 200 m visibility | compliant |\n| `idle` | bicycle at rest | not applicable |\n| `blind` | visibility masked | unknown |\n| `branch_1` | ice, 40 m visibility; the dry stopping distance would fit | violated |\n| `branch_2` (added) | wet road, 29 m visibility; dry would comply | violated |\n| `branch_3` (added) | precipitation only, road not flagged wet; dry would comply | violated |\n| `branch_4` (added) | darkness, 200 m visibility; the 30 m headlamp reach decides | violated |\n\nI added `branch_2` to `branch_4` so that the wet-road, precipitation and darkness conditions each change at least one witness's verdict, as the gate requires.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
